\title{castSDM: Model Response and Interventional Effects for Species Distribution Models}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Audits model-based environmental responses in species distribution modelling. A single raw-unit predictor shift evaluated over a fitted model produces a shift effect size and a spatial effect map with hard range-masking. Variable selection is a two-stage screen whose second stage ranks predictors by a conditional effect that holds other predictors fixed, calibrated against a conditional-permutation null. The effect products carry a hard range diagnostic: rows or cells outside the training quantile box are masked, not ranked. This does not establish conditional positivity or causal identification. The package provides a complete workflow - Random Forest, BRT, MaxEnt and GAM learners, nested spatial cross-validation, ensemble prediction, and future climate projection with extrapolation control. The package targets interpretable interventional attribution under stated assumptions. Outputs do not establish ecological causality or convert presence-background suitability to occurrence probability.
}
